.TH TIMED 8 "Peios" "timed 0.1.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
timed \- Peios authenticated network time client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/timed
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timed
keeps the system clock synchronised with configured network sources.  It is
the only service granted
.B SeSystemtimePrivilege
in the standard Peios image.  The daemon initiates NTP and Network Time
Security connections but listens on no network port.
.PP
At startup it raises a clock older than the reproducible build timestamp to
that timestamp.  This conservative floor permits certificate validation on a
machine with an absent or failed real-time clock; it is not considered a
successful time synchronisation.
.PP
Network Time Security is required by default.  Plain NTP is used only when an
administrator explicitly enables it for a source.  Source selection requires
agreement and rejects outliers rather than allowing a preferred source to
override the majority.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon watches
.B Machine\\System\\Time
in the Peios registry.  Important values are:
.TP
.B Servers
A REG_MULTI_SZ list of hosts, optionally followed by
.B prefer
or
.BR unauthenticated .
.TP
.B AllowUnauthenticated
A REG_DWORD enabling explicitly marked plain-NTP sources.  The secure default
is zero.
.TP
.B UseFromDHCP
A REG_DWORD allowing DHCP option 42 when no explicit source list exists.  The
secure default is zero.
.TP
.BR MinPoll , " MaxPoll"
REG_DWORD base-two polling intervals, bounded by the daemon.
.PP
Complete field semantics and security notes are installed as the
.B timed.regman
registry manual.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/timed/time.sock
Local query and control socket.
.TP
.B /var/state/timed/drift
Persisted learned oscillator frequency.
.TP
.B /var/state/timed/cookies/
Persisted NTS cookies.  This directory is private to SYSTEM,
Administrators, and timed's service SID.
.SH SERVICE INTEGRATION
The package supplies inert Registry Image Manager seeds for the service,
time policy, and the service-SID privilege grant.  An image must explicitly
select those seeds.  The service runs as LocalService; its pre-start hook runs
as SYSTEM only to provision the protected state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clock (1),
.BR reg (1),
.BR svctl (1)
